[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihv2TK04WPg"]
[Date "2021.06.21"]
[Round "1"]
[White "White repertoire"]
[Black "e6 Sicilian"]
[Result "*"]
[Annotator "GM Daniel Naroditsky videos"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: French / Taimanov / Kan"]
[SourceTitle "Master Class | Open Sicilian | Chess Speedrun | Grandmaster Naroditsky"]
[SourceURL "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihv2TK04WPg"]

1. Nf3 c5
2. e4 e6
(2... Qc7
{Early queen/Kan move order. Keep normal Open Sicilian development.}
3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 a6
5. Nc3 e6
6. Bd3)
3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 Nf6
5. Bd3
{Weak-deck reference. `Bd3` defends e4, prepares castling, and aims at h7 before Black gets comfortable `...d5` play.}
5... Nc6
6. Nxc6
{Damage the queenside structure and choose a plan instead of memorizing a huge Taimanov tree.}
6... bxc6
7. O-O d5
8. e5 Nd7
9. Re1 Be7
10. Qg4
{Plan: use the e5 space, bring a rook to e1, and create kingside questions before Black's bishops coordinate.} *

[Event "Weak Opening GM Lesson - Kan and Drazic Move Orders"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihv2TK04WPg"]
[Date "2021.06.21"]
[Round "2"]
[White "White repertoire"]
[Black "Kan / Drazic"]
[Result "*"]
[Annotator "GM Daniel Naroditsky video"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Kan / Drazic"]

1. Nf3 c5
2. e4 a6
3. d4 e6
4. Nc3
{The weak deck flags this as the reference against early `...a6`: develop the knight and keep an Open Sicilian center.}
4... cxd4
5. Nxd4 Qc7
6. Bd3 Nf6
7. O-O d6
8. Qe2 Be7
{You have reached a Kan/Scheveningen shell. Develop first; then choose f4, Be3, or c4 depending on Black's setup.} *

[Event "Weak Opening GM Lesson - Nc6 d6 and Bc4 Open Sicilian"]
[Site "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihv2TK04WPg"]
[Date "2021.06.21"]
[Round "3"]
[White "White repertoire"]
[Black "Nc6 / d6 Sicilian"]
[Result "*"]
[Annotator "GM Daniel Naroditsky video"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Open"]

1. Nf3 c5
2. e4 Nc6
3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 Nf6
5. Nc3 d6
(5... e5
{Sveshnikov/Lasker-Pelikan branch.}
6. Ndb5 d6
7. Bg5 a6
8. Na3 b5
9. Bxf6 Qxf6
10. Nd5
{The weak-deck `Bg5` idea: trade the f6 knight when useful and occupy d5.})
6. Bc4
{Weak-deck reference. Develop actively, pressure f7 and d5, and make Black prove the center is safe.}
6... e6
7. Bb3 Be7
8. O-O O-O
9. Be3
{Healthy Open Sicilian setup: bishop on b3, castle, Be3, Qe2/Qf3, and rooks to d1/e1 depending on Black's center.} *

